01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:08,500
Bones and All is a 2022 romantic horror film directed by Luca Guadagnino from a screenplay by
David Kajganich, based on the 2015 novel Bones & All by Camille DeAngelis.

12
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
Set in the late 1980s, the film stars Taylor Russell and Timothée Chalamet as a pair of young
cannibals who develop feelings for each other on a road trip across the United States.

13
01:10:57,500 --> 01:11:03,500
Michael Stuhlbarg, André Holland, Chloë Sevigny, David Gordon Green, Jessica
Harper, Jake Horowitz, and Mark Rylance appear in supporting roles.

14
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:31,000
Bones and All had its world premiere at the 79th Venice International Film Festival on September 2, 2022,
where it won the Silver Lion for best direction and the Marcello Mastroianni Award for Russell.

15
01:21:52,500 --> 01:21:58,500
The film was released theatrically in the United States on November 18 by United Artists
Releasing's Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Pictures, and elsewhere by Warner Bros.

16
